 ],
 "article": {
  "title": "The Science of Music: Why Songs Move Us",
  "topic": "艺术·音乐与大脑",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "words": 305,
  "paras": [
   "Music is everywhere — in lifts, on phones, and in the background of shops and airports. Yet few of us stop to ask why a simple melody can make us cry, dance, or suddenly remember a summer long past. For thousands of years, music has been part of human life, but only recently have scientists begun to understand what it really does to the brain.",
   "Using brain scans, researchers have found that music stimulates far more than the hearing area. Rhythm activates the parts of the brain that control movement, which is why we find it hard to stay still when a good beat plays. Melody and harmony light up regions linked to emotion, and familiar songs wake up the memory centres as well. In other words, when we listen to music, almost the whole brain joins in. No wonder a good song can lift a dull day or calm a racing heart.",
   "This may explain why learning an instrument is so good for us. Studies suggest that children who practise music regularly do better in memory and attention tasks. For adults, playing or singing can reduce stress and even slow certain effects of ageing. Music also has a social power: singing in a choir or dancing at a festival helps people feel connected, because doing something in time with others builds trust and understanding.",
   "Of course, tastes differ. What sounds beautiful to one person may sound like noise to another, and this, too, is shaped by culture and experience. Still, the basic response is universal: human beings are musical creatures from birth. So the next time a song moves you, remember that it is not just art — it is your brain, body and memory working together."
  ],
  "zh": "音乐无处不在，但很少有人想过一段旋律为何能让我们落泪、起舞或想起某个久远的夏天。脑成像研究发现，音乐不只刺激听觉区：节奏会激活控制运动的脑区，旋律与和声则点亮与情绪相关的区域，熟悉的歌还会唤醒记忆中枢——听音乐时几乎整个大脑都在参与。这也解释了为何学乐器有益：常练音乐的孩子在记忆与注意力任务中表现更好，成年人演奏或歌唱能减压、延缓衰老，而合唱、共舞等“与别人合拍”的行为还能增进信任与联结。当然，口味因人而异，但这种基本反应是普遍的——人天生就是热爱音乐的生物。",
  "hard": [
   {
    "en": "Rhythm activates the parts of the brain that control movement, which is why we find it hard to stay still when a good beat plays.",
    "cn": "节奏会激活大脑中控制运动的区域，这就是为什么当好的节拍响起时，我们很难保持不动。",
    "why": "主句后接 that 引导的定语从句修饰 parts，再由 which 引导非限定从句指代前面整句、表示结果，when 引导时间状语从句。写作时可模仿“..., which is why ...”来承接结果。"
   },
   {
    "en": "Studies suggest that children who practise music regularly do better in memory and attention tasks.",
    "cn": "研究表明，经常练习音乐的儿童在记忆和注意力任务中表现更好。",
    "why": "suggest that 引导宾语从句，从句内 who 引导定语从句修饰 children。仿写模板：“Studies suggest that people who ... tend to ...”很适合议论文举证据。"
   }
  ],
